| `bb test:cljs` | **1215 tests, 34280 assertions, 0 failures, 0 warnings** (was 34262) |

`Testing dao.stream.slice-test` present at line 119 of both full logs. The slice namespace alone went from 77 to 96 assertions on the JVM.

**Negative controls** — both fixes were the kind that pass vacuously, so I proved they bite. Inverting `(is (some? terminal))` and pointing `logical-identity` at a constant produced **8 failures on each host, identically**: 4 showing the asserted histories really do contain `:ws/closed` with the correct attachment UUIDs (client and server, both attachments), and 4 showing all four identity projections are checked against the real minted value (`cca85bfc-…` on the JVM, `82024812-…` on Node). Both files were then restored and re-verified clean — no `NEGATIVE-CONTROL` or `nil? terminal` markers remain.

Nothing staged or committed. cljd was not re-run; these edits are to `.clj`/`.cljs` files the Dart build doesn't see.
